
Build the package from source:
$ ./make-debian.sh

Copy it to the SD card:
$ sudo cp hobart-valgrind.pkg /media/hobart/hobart/root

You need the debugging ld.so on your target SD card (with symbols)! Copy it from the toolchain:
$ sudo cp /opt/hb6mxd_combo/toolchain/lib/ld-2.19.so /media/hobart/hobart/lib


Boot the sd card and install the package:
# dpkg -i /root/hobart-valgrind.pkg

Run valigrind with correct SO path:
# VALGRIND_LIB=/usr/lib/valgrind valgrind chobart_d

For full memory checking use the following flag:
# VALGRIND_LIB=/usr/lib/valgrind valgrind  --leak-check=full chobart_d



Log valgrind output to a file:
# VALGRIND_LIB=/usr/lib/valgrind valgrind --log-file="log.txt" chobart_d

--error-limit=no

--undef-value-errors=no

Log valgrind output and app output to file.
# VALGRIND_LIB=/usr/lib/valgrind valgrind chobart_d > log.txt 2>&1
